# ERA — common laws (all systems)

Inherits nothing; app-specific rules add detail on top. User chat — **Russian**. Code, comments, commits, repo docs — **English**.

## Source of truth

| Layer | Where |
|-------|--------|
| Product / scope | Each app's `PRD.md` / `TZ.md` — attach `@PRD.md`, `@TZ.md` for nontrivial work |
| Cross-cutting architecture | `docs/adr/`, `docs/CONTROL_PLANE_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/INTEGRATION_SSO_EVENTS.md` |
| Ports / URLs | `docs/ECOSYSTEM_URLS.md` |
| Doc upkeep | Root `documentation-upkeep.mdc` |

## Multi-tenancy

- **Finance + Orchestrator:** tenant-scoped models use `organizationId`; Prisma tenant extension; raw SQL must filter by org; BullMQ jobs carry tenant from payload (or documented global-only jobs).
- **Industry satellites (target):** same `organizationId` discipline. Topology (`SHARED` / `DEDICATED` / `ONPREM`) is placement — [deployment-topology.md](../../docs/adr/deployment-topology.md). Do not treat “one deployment = one org” as the schema law.
- **Industry satellites (today):** many tables still omit `organizationId` (Nafta appliance = DEDICATED/ONPREM). New tenant tables and uniques must be org-scoped. Do not capture `ERA_SATELLITE_ORGANIZATION_ID` at module import — use `satelliteOrganizationId()` / runtime config.
- **Outlet** = point of sale inside one org; **DEPARTMENT/STANDALONE** = legal/money; never use those words for VM topology.
- **Person identity:** satellites store `globalPersonId` only; PII lives in MDM (`era_mdm`). Do not duplicate FIN/passport in satellite DBs when MDM-linked.

## Security

- **NestJS apps:** global `ValidationPipe` — `whitelist: true`, `forbidNonWhitelisted: true`, `transform: true`.
- **Mutations** (POST/PATCH/PUT/DELETE): audit trail where the app supports it (Finance `AuditMutationInterceptor`; satellites — equivalent or documented exceptions for auth/public).
- **Internal / event APIs:** `Authorization: Bearer` service token (`SATELLITE_EVENT_SERVICE_TOKEN`, MDM internal token). Do not leave write endpoints unauthenticated in production paths.
- No loose `any` on API inputs; use DTO + `class-validator` / Zod.

## Compliance (Azerbaijan)

- Currency **AZN**; phone **+994**; legal entity **VÖEN** (10 digits); citizen **FIN** (7 chars, no I/O) when applicable.
- Foreigners: passport + `issuingCountry` as alternate identifier; FIN optional until residency.
- Dates: **UTC in DB**; display in **Asia/Baku** locale where user-facing.

## Data integrity

- Ledger, stock+GL, payroll posting, invoice payment/netting, fiscal issuance — **atomic transactions** (`prisma.$transaction` or equivalent).
- Money routing respects org operating mode (`shouldRouteRevenueToParent`, `shouldFiscalizeOnParent` from `@era/satellite-kit`).

## Code placement

- Domain logic in **services**, not controllers/route handlers (thin HTTP layer).
- Cross-satellite contracts in **`packages/era-contracts`**; shared satellite behavior in **`packages/satellite-kit`**.
- Do not add parallel app roots without updating TZ/ADR.
